<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset='utf-8'><style>body{font-family:Arial;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.25}h1{text-align:center;font-size:18pt}h2{font-size:13pt;margin-bottom:3px}ol{margin-top:3px}li{margin:3px 0}</style></head><body>
<h1>Use-Case Flow Specification</h1><p><b>Use Case:</b> UC-03 Search Compatible Rides and Request to Join</p><p><b>Primary actor:</b> Rider Commuter &nbsp; <b>Supporting actor:</b> Carpooling Portal / Driver Host</p>
<h2>Preconditions</h2><ul><li>Rider is registered and authenticated.</li><li>At least one origin, destination, and travel date are available as search inputs.</li><li>Driver rides may be published and have available seats.</li></ul>
<h2>Postconditions</h2><p>A compatible ride-join request is stored with status <b>Pending</b>, and the Driver Host is notified. No seat is reserved until the driver accepts.</p>
<h2>Main Success Scenario</h2><ol><li>Rider selects <i>Find a ride</i> and enters origin, destination, date, and optional departure window.</li><li>System validates the inputs and geocodes the locations.</li><li>System compares the rider route with published driver routes, applying the 1.5 km maximum detour rule.</li><li>System displays compatible rides with driver rating, departure time, available seats, estimated detour, and estimated fuel share.</li><li>Rider selects a ride and reviews its details and cost split.</li><li>Rider selects <i>Request to join</i>.</li><li>System verifies that the ride is not full and records the request as <b>Pending</b>.</li><li>System sends an in-app notification to the Driver Host and confirmation to the Rider.</li><li>Use case ends; the rider can view the pending request in <i>My trips</i>.</li></ol>
<h2>Alternate Flow: No Compatible Ride (3a)</h2><ol><li>At step 3, no published ride satisfies the route, date, or 1.5 km detour constraint.</li><li>System displays “No compatible rides found” and offers the rider options to widen the departure window, save the search, or try another date.</li><li>If the rider changes criteria, the flow returns to step 2; otherwise the use case ends without creating a request.</li></ol>
<h2>Alternate Flow: Ride Becomes Full (6a)</h2><p>Before recording the request, the system detects that all seats were taken. It displays an unavailable message and returns the rider to the results list.</p>
</body></html>
